1
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:40,160
CONVERSATION 1
I’ve just bought a new blender.

2
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:41,200
What’s that?

3
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:45,080
A blender, you know, a machine that blends food.

4
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:46,760
Ah, yes, of course.

5
00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:48,680
The electric kitchen appliance.

6
00:00:48,680 --> 00:00:49,800
Exactly.

7
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:52,100
This one is state of the art.

8
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:57,960
I’ve been meaning to buy one for a while and I did thorough research on which specific model to get.

9
00:00:57,960 --> 00:01:01,400
I read through maybe hundreds of online user reviews.

10
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:03,180
Anyway, it’s amazing.

11
00:01:03,180 --> 00:01:03,740
Really?

12
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:05,560
What could be so special about it?

13
00:01:05,560 --> 00:01:07,500
I mean, it’s just a blender.

14
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:10,520
Well, basically, it’s just a very good one.

15
00:01:10,520 --> 00:01:13,540
It feels heavy and sturdy and well-made.

16
00:01:13,540 --> 00:01:18,520
It also has lots of power and can easily cut and crush practically anything.

17
00:01:18,520 --> 00:01:24,560
This way, the soups and juices I make come out really fine and smooth, with no lumpy bits.

18
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:26,260
Hmm, I see.

19
00:01:26,260 --> 00:01:28,420
I’ve never thought of getting one myself.

20
00:01:28,420 --> 00:01:33,540
It sounds like the kind of thing that, for me personally, I would rarely use.

21
00:01:33,540 --> 00:01:34,820
I’ve never had one before.

22
00:01:34,820 --> 00:01:37,800
And now that I do, I use it all the time.

23
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:45,760
I make a fresh fruit juice in the morning, maybe not every morning, but three or four times a week, and it feels fantastic.

24
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:46,820
It’s a really healthy habit.

25
00:01:46,820 --> 00:01:50,940
I can imagine that must feel quite satisfying.

26
00:01:50,940 --> 00:01:56,860
I can picture you getting all creative in the kitchen and trying out a multitude of different ingredients.

27
00:01:56,860 --> 00:02:02,200
And it’s obviously going to be healthier than buying packaged juice from a supermarket.

28
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:03,800
It’s so much healthier.

29
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:05,340
It’s not even close.

30
00:02:05,340 --> 00:02:09,360
Did you know that store-bought juice is like 10% sugar?

31
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:10,060
Right.

32
00:02:10,060 --> 00:02:12,240
So then you bought it for the health benefits?

33
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:14,840
Mostly yes.

34
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:19,880
Basically, it allows me to have a more varied diet with a far wider assortment of nutrients.

35
00:02:19,880 --> 00:02:36,480
Because it’s not only fruit in my morning juices you see, I can also throw in vegetables, nuts, yogurts, cereals, anything that tickles my fancy.

36
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:54,440
Q1. What does the man say he did before buying the blender?

37
00:02:54,440 --> 00:03:11,940
Q2. What does the woman say she has never thought of doing?

38
00:03:11,940 --> 00:03:29,260
Q3. What does the man say is a really healthy habit?

39
00:03:29,260 --> 00:03:48,120
Q4. What do we learn about store-bought juice from the conversation?

40
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:51,480
CONVERSATION 2
Today we have a very interesting guest.

41
00:03:51,480 --> 00:04:00,440
Mr. Thomas Benjamin Grimm, the mayor of Berkton, is here to talk about his job and responsibilities, overseeing this charming village.

42
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:02,780
Mr. Grimm, thank you for being here.

43
00:04:02,780 --> 00:04:04,460
Thank you for having me.

44
00:04:04,460 --> 00:04:07,220
I’d like to start by stating the obvious.

45
00:04:07,220 --> 00:04:13,720
Berkton has become one of the most popular tourist destinations in the country, and this has happened under your watch.

46
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:16,260
Just how did you achieve this?

47
00:04:16,260 --> 00:04:19,640
The achievement belongs to all the residents of Berkton.

48
00:04:19,640 --> 00:04:23,660
It was a shared effort, where everybody pitched in for the communal good.

49
00:04:23,660 --> 00:04:25,500
But how did this change happen?

50
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:33,160
In about 10 years, Berkton has gone from a relatively unheard-of sleepy village to a must-see destination.

51
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:36,720
Yes, the change has truly been remarkable.

52
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:41,600
Berkton was always fortunate to be endowed with such a beautiful natural allure.

53
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:49,560
The Embry Hills above the village remain untouched by human development, and the Sonora Valley, just below it, is equally stunning.

54
00:04:49,560 --> 00:05:01,380
The transformation commenced in a town hall meeting in spring 2008, over 10 years ago now, when an overwhelming majority of neighbours voted in favor of Motion 836.

55
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:08,500
This legislative proposal essentially set out to harmonize the aesthetic appearance of all the houses in Berkton.

56
00:05:08,500 --> 00:05:17,180
The idea was that if all the properties looked a certain way with shared design features, then a village as a whole would look more beautiful.

57
00:05:17,180 --> 00:05:18,820
And it worked.

58
00:05:18,820 --> 00:05:20,360
It certainly did.

59
00:05:20,360 --> 00:05:25,880
I’m looking now at a before-and-after photo, and the change is truly remarkable.

60
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:28,280
It’s hard to believe it’s the same place.

61
00:05:28,280 --> 00:05:30,460
And how do the neighbours feel now?

62
00:05:30,460 --> 00:05:31,980
Great pride, I would say.

63
00:05:31,980 --> 00:05:36,540
But what about the multitudes of visitors now crowding the streets?

64
00:05:36,540 --> 00:05:38,880
Is everyone happy about that?

65
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:44,600
The tourists we receive are a blessing as they have completely revitalized the local economy.

66
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:53,660
Every visitor is warmly welcome.

67
00:05:53,660 --> 00:06:12,560
Q5. What is the question the woman asked Mr. Grimm after the introduction?

68
00:06:12,560 --> 00:06:30,060
Q6. What do we learn about Berkton of 10 years ago?

69
00:06:30,060 --> 00:06:50,760
Q7. What resulted from the passing of the legislative proposal Motion 836?

70
00:06:50,760 --> 00:07:41,240
Q8. Why does the man say the tourists are a blessing to Berkton?

71
00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:48,780
